**[SUGGESTION Simplification]** In the einsum fallback, `self.linear_o_group_proj` is already stored as a 3D parameter of shape `(o_local_groups, o_lora_rank, group_proj_in_size)` (see `__init__`, lines 207-210), and `_load_from_state_dict` also normalizes any loaded 2D checkpoint back to `self._linear_o_group_proj_weight.shape` (3D). So this `.reshape(o_local_groups, o_lora_rank, -1)` is a no-op that runs on every forward pass.

You can drop it and pass the weight straight into the einsum:

```python
def _apply_linear_o_group_proj(self, input_: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:
    """Apply TE BatchedLinear when available, otherwise use the legacy einsum."""
    if self._uses_te_batched_linear:
        return self.linear_o_group_proj(input_)
    return torch.einsum("...gd,grd->...gr", input_, self._linear_o_group_proj_weight)
```

Minor — purely a readability/tidiness cleanup, no behavioral change.

